export { setRenderTaskGpuTimingEnabled, isRenderTaskGpuTimingSupported, getRenderTaskGpuTimings } from "./engine/gpu-task-timing.js";
```

This was load-bearing because it reveals the fundamental API shift: Babylon Lite uses a functional/imperative API (`createEngine`, `renderFrame`, etc.) rather than the class-based OOP API (`new Engine()`, `scene.render()`) that Babylon.js uses. This is a key architectural difference.

